Article 33
(1) The fulfillment of children's rights is implemented in an integrated and systematic manner from all sectors on a sustainable basis through the KLA development policy.
- 15­ (2) The KLA development policy as referred to in paragraph (1) contains provisions regarding:
a. the KLA concept;
b. children's rights; and
c. the KLA development approach.
(3) The KLA development policy as referred to in paragraph (1) is directed toward the fulfillment of children's rights, comprising:
a. civil rights and freedoms;
b. family environment and alternative care;
c. basic health and welfare;
d. education, utilization of leisure time, and cultural activities; and
e. special protection.
(4) The stages of KLA development as referred to in paragraph (1), comprise:
a. preparation;
b. planning;
c. implementation;
d. monitoring;
e. evaluation; and
f. reporting.
(5) Further provisions regarding the KLA development policy shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

Article 2
Protection of women and children victims of violence is conducted based on the principles of:
a. respect and fulfillment of victims' rights;
b. justice and gender equality;
c. non-discrimination;
d. the best interests of victims; and
e. empowerment.

Article 34
(1) In order to ensure the effectiveness of the implementation of KLA development policy in the Region, a KLA Task Force shall be established.
(2) The KLA Task Force as referred to in paragraph (1), shall have the following principal duties, namely:
a. coordinating the implementation of KLA policy and development;
b. determining the tasks of the members of the KLA Task Force;
c. conducting socialization, advocacy and communication of information and education on KLA policy;
d. collecting baseline data;
e. conducting needs analysis sourced from baseline data;
f. conducting dissemination of baseline data;
g. determining the focus and priority of programs in realizing KLA, which shall be adjusted to the potential of the Region;
h. preparing a regional action plan and KLA working mechanism for 5 (five) years; and
i. conducting monitoring, evaluation and reporting at least once every 1 (one) year.
(3) Further provisions regarding the procedures for appointment and dismissal of membership of the KLA Task Force shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

